  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A logic gate gives the reversible operation&nbsp;if&nbsp;we can recover input data from the output.</p><p>For example, a NOT gate gives the reversible operation because we always know that the input is the reverse of the output.</p><p>For the given logic gate, let the input is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>.</p><p>So, the output,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>X</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;(NOT gate)</p>",
    "image": null
